{
  "_comment": [
    "Validate-mode golden: design §5.4's noexcept ↔ *Throws:*",
    "cross-check, over hand-written IR (no Clang needed, so this runs on",
    "every lane).",
    "",
    "Two positives. `has_value` is declared `noexcept` and carries an",
    "authored `\\throws` saying it throws -- the contradiction. `reset` is",
    "declared `noexcept` and carries a `\\throws` reading `Nothing.` --",
    "true, but already said by the signature, and not something the draft",
    "writes.",
    "",
    "Both are Warnings, and this case is registered with EXPECT_EXIT 0 to",
    "pin that: an Error makes `render --validate` skip rendering, so the",
    "answer to a wrong *Throws:* paragraph would be no wording at all.",
    "",
    "There is no reverse-direction case here because there is no reverse",
    "direction: a *Throws:* reading `Nothing` on a signature that is *not*",
    "`noexcept` is correct and common, since the Lakos Rule keeps a",
    "narrow-contract function un-`noexcept` so that checking its",
    "precondition and throwing stays in bounds. `front` below is that",
    "shape, as a control.",
    "",
    "Seven negative controls, which must stay silent alongside those two:",
    "`value` is not `noexcept` at all, so its `\\throws` is ordinary;",
    "`front` is the Lakos-Rule shape just described -- narrow contract, not",
    "`noexcept`, `\\throws Nothing.`;",
    "`swap`'s specification is conditional, so it may throw; `at`'s two",
    "grouped overloads disagree, and the authored wording may be describing",
    "the one that can throw; `probe`'s only `noexcept` belongs to a",
    "function-pointer parameter, inside the parameter list rather than on",
    "the function; `risky` is `noexcept(false)`, which says it may throw;",
    "and `clear` is `noexcept(true)` with no `\\throws` at all.",
    "",
    "`clear`'s sibling `flush` is the `noexcept(true)` positive: the spelling",
    "has to read the same as bare `noexcept`, which only a case pairing it",
    "with a contradicting `\\throws` can show."
  ],
